! POWHEG-BOX-RES (DIS_v), NEUTRINO CHARGED CURRENT: 1 TeV nu_mu on a proton
! at rest.  The cross-check partner of POWHEG-V2 on the neutrino side.
!
! >>> INCLUSIVE PRODUCTION ONLY.  THIS SAMPLE MUST NOT BE USED FOR CHARM. <<<
! DIS_v/init_processes.f hardcodes
!       CKM_diag = .true.
! in three places, with no input keyword to change it, so only same-generation
! transitions are generated: s -> c is present, and d -> c is ABSENT
! altogether.  The CKM matrix is not merely diagonal, it is unused -- the
! ph_CKM_matrix built in init_couplings.f is consumed nowhere, and Born.f and
! real.f contain no CKM at all, despite a comment promising that "CKM matrix
! elements will be added when the event is written on the Les Houches file".
!
! On the INCLUSIVE rate this is largely harmless: CKM unitarity means moving
! weight between d -> c and d -> u leaves the sum nearly unchanged, which is
! the same argument that made Sherpa's unit-CKM NLO run usable inclusively.
! On the CHARM COMPOSITION it is not: the identical defect in Sherpa cost
! 3.4 points on the charm fraction (18.69% against the correct 22.10%), and
! that is why Sherpa's virtual-ME getter was patched rather than worked
! around.  There is no equivalent patch here, so this run is generated,
! analysed and reported for the inclusive selection alone.
!
! Conventions otherwise identical to ../mu1TeV-wide: NNPDF4.0 NNLO,
! muF = muR = Q, Gmu EW, massless quarks.
!
! VALIDATED against POWHEG-V2 on the same wide generation region:
!     POWHEG-RES  btilde 4.031 + remnants 0.447 = 4.478 pb
!     POWHEG-V2                                   4.454 pb
! i.e. 0.5% apart -- which is the point, and also the evidence for the caveat
! above: the inclusive rate agrees BECAUSE CKM unitarity protects it, while
! the charm composition, which unitarity does not protect, is where the
! diagonal-CKM restriction would show.

numevts 60000        ! events per seed; 10 seeds -> 600k total

ih1 14               ! lepton beam: nu_mu (|ih1| in {12,14,16} -> neutrino beam)
ih2  1               ! hadron 2 (1 for protons)
ebeam1 1000d0        ! neutrino beam energy [GeV]
ebeam2 0.938d0       ! proton at rest (mass)
fixed_lepton_beam 1  ! single fixed-energy lepton beam
fixed_target 1       ! beam 2 at rest, mass = ebeam2

bornktmin 0d0
bornsuppfact 0d0     ! no Born suppression: flat event weights

Qmin 1.5d0           ! generation cut Q2 > 2.25: safely below the analysis cut Q2 > 4,
                     ! so radiation can migrate INTO the fiducial region (leptonic
                     ! Q2 > 4 with Born Q2 < 4); cutting at generation Q2=4 biased
                     ! sigma_fid low by ~1%
Qmax 10000d0
xmin 0d0
xmax 1d0
ymin 0d0
ymax 1d0

lhans1   331100      ! NNPDF40_nnlo_as_01180
lhans2   331100
alphas_from_pdf 1

renscfact  1d0
facscfact  1d0
runningscales 1      ! muF = muR = Q

channel_type 3       ! ALL CHARGED-CURRENT channels (4 would be NC)
vtype 3              ! (NC-only switch; inert with channel_type 3)
smartsig 1
nores 1
olddij 0

! EW parameters: Gmu-scheme values used as fixed couplings (matched to Sherpa)
alphaem 0.0075689340670153d0   ! 1/132.119
s2w 0.22291d0

muonmass 0.10566d0   ! the OUTGOING lepton of CC nu_mu DIS is a mu-

use-old-grid    1
use-old-ubound  1

ncall1 50000         ! calls per process for importance-sampling grid
itmx1 1              ! (xgriditerations handled by parallel stage 1)
ncall2 50000         ! calls per process for upper-bounding envelope
itmx2 1
foldcsi 5
foldy   5
foldphi 1
nubound 50000
iupperfsr 1

fastbtlbound 1
storemintupb 1
ubexcess_correct 1
storeinfo_rwgt 1
hdamp 0
bornzerodamp 1

withnegweights 1
flg_jacsing 1
testplots 0

xupbound 2d0
iseed    12
manyseeds 1
doublefsr 0

parallelstage 4
xgriditeration 1
